## Item SA-F3 (S1) — FIXED

Root cause (code-cited): the run loop's marquee "steady ticker" pin
branch compared `marquee_next_step(now) <= now` — but next_step is
STRICTLY FUTURE by construction (k = q+1 ⇒ start+k·80 > now), so the
pin NEVER fired. The clock advanced only on the plain 100ms branch;
wakes landed on every 80ms boundary, so the 100ms threshold tripped
every OTHER boundary → the clock jumped +160ms → offset +2 cells per
render → the measured ~166ms/step.

- marquee.rs: `passed_step_ms` — the most recent boundary ≤ now while
  the scroll is live (liveness mirrors next_step_ms; None past the
  one-pass clamp). Unit test pins the invariant pair (next is strictly
  future; pin+interval = next) and the clamp symmetry.
- session_tabs_solid.rs: `marquee_passed_step` accessor.
- app.rs tick section: while a scroll is live, wake → pin
  `advance_clock(passed_boundary)` when newer than the clock (compared
  against the CLOCK, never `now`); the plain 100ms tick stays suspended
  while scrolling (the 80ms pin cadence subsumes it — the clock never
  samples past a boundary the marquee should land on).
- vt_temporal.rs marquee test upgraded to the SA-F3 vt-clock proof:
  polls the LIVE grid every 12ms (the snapshot instrument's 80ms
  quiet window CANNOT resolve an 80ms cadence — consecutive frames
  merge into one burst; direct grid polling measures change times),
  takes the longest ≤300ms-separated steady run, asserts median ∈
  [70,105], max ≤ 140 (no ~166 quantization leak), min ≥ 55 (no
  double-steps), ≥10 shifts. MEASURED: 27 shifts, median 77ms, min
  76, max 90 (3/3 stable + full vt_temporal suite 5/5 PASS — the
  100ms-cadence surfaces unchanged).
